WEBVTT

NOTE Narration by an AI voice: Matilda (XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX), eleven_v4.

intro
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:09.140
Copilot measures a slow SPL2 search, then asks Splunk AI Assistant to optimize it.

full-baseline
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.400
Here is the complete original search, with no hidden clauses or abbreviated code.

separate-counts
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.460
The baseline counts attempts, then counts failures in a second branch.

join
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.660
Both branches start broadly, then a join matches their counts by service and version.

unused-eval
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:37.540
The original also computes a failure indicator without using it, then renames the joined fields.

extra-work
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.440
That is extra work for a report that needs only grouped attempts and failures.

skill
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.040
The performance skill compares job metrics with query structure.

authorization
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.180
Only search jobs are authorized; no Splunk configuration changes are needed.

measure
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.680
Copilot submits the original search, then waits for its completed-job status.

evidence
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.900
The actual result rows become the reference for checking the rewrite.

baseline
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.700
The baseline takes about one hundred forty-eight seconds to return four rows.

request
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:23.060
Copilot asks Splunk AI Assistant for a valid, more efficient SPL2 query.

preserve
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.500
The request preserves the report's fields and calculations, without adding a time filter.

scope
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:36.260
Narrowing an index is useful only when it still covers the data the report needs.

compare-not-guess
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.700
A shorter query is not enough; its result values must still match.

full-rewrite
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:51.480
SAIA replaces wildcard index selection with the sample-data index.

single-aggregation
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.500
One aggregation counts all attempts and sums failures directly from the same events.

removed-work
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.940
The separate failure search and join are gone.

verify-next
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.140
Copilot now runs this exact rewrite to check the improvement.

matching-rows
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:18.260
The comparison checks every service and version, not just the number of output rows.

measured-not-guaranteed
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.920
These are measured runtimes for this run; caching and load can affect other runs.

runtime
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.020
Runtime drops to about eight seconds, roughly nineteen times faster.

parity
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:39.100
All four rows match in value; tied rows can appear in a different order.

diff-legend
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.940
Red marks removals, green additions, yellow changes.

diff-removals
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:53.420
Original left, rewrite right: two searches become one aggregation.

same-report
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000
The rate calculation and report fields stay the same.

close
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.200
Same failure-rate report, delivered in seconds.
